## Second pass (14 October 2026): M21 typed-transition classifier, and the quiet side of a flash

**What was added.** M21 (`zrmd/analyze/rhythm_ramps.py`, `Scripts/RhythmRamps.py`): candidate spans from six loose generators (fade through a flat run, cross-dissolve, sharpness-collapse whip, flat run of any colour, a group of two or three predicted cuts, a run of steps above 0.03), one 44-column evidence vector per candidate, one ensemble of 300 trees of depth 5, non-maximum suppression, V1 gates before it. Four phases, pooled over the eleven references, fin-4 and the four synthetic videos (70 adjudicated transitions, 16 of them on real references). FR : M21, le classifieur des transitions typees, quatre phases. (14 October 2026)

| phase | what is measured | result |
|---|---|---|
| P1 signal | does a RIGHT answer exist among the candidates (instant inside the adjudicated interval, span not much wider, no true cut swallowed, every predicted cut inside covered)? | real references 16 of 16, synthetic videos 46 of 54 |
| P2 candidates | candidates per video, all kinds | 0 to 330 (fin-4 0, memo 270, x-anabology-2105 272); 1 514 in the training set, 160 of them right answers |
| P3 verify | classifier score, resubstitution: right answers 0.9966 and above, every other candidate 0.019 and below | tp / fp / fn 60 / 1 / 10 (F1 0.916), real references 16 / 0 / 0 |
| P4 place | the instant of a kept span against the adjudicated interval, leave-one-video-out at confidence 0.99 | tp / fp / fn 24 / 1 / 46 (F1 0.505), real references 2 / 1 / 14 (F1 0.211) |

Against the threshold detectors M16 to M18 pooled over the same videos (38 / 56 / 32, F1 0.463), the classifier trades recall for precision held out (0.96 against 0.40), which is the right trade for a typed event that also removes the cuts under it. **What it is worth, said plainly:** the all-kinds leave-one-reference-out F1 of the product moves from 0.8610 (micro) and 0.8422 (macro) before the pass to 0.8640 and 0.8425 after it; at the naive confidence 0.5 it costs (0.8599 and 0.8327), it is neutral from 0.9 to 0.99 and the shipped 0.99 was chosen on those same numbers. In resubstitution every reference reaches 1.000. (14 October 2026)

**Flash, quiet side (14 October 2026).** A flash needs a quiet side: the picture before an entry is calm (quiet before at most 0.7) and the picture after an exit settles (quiet after at most 0.7). On the boundaries the first-pass leave-one-out probabilities typed as flashes (x-anabology-2105, 16) the entries measure at most 0.47 and the exits at most 0.09; memo 858 measures 0.95 and is a cut again. Zero flash lost, one cut gained, and the same eight boundaries are typed with the retrained fusion. (14 October 2026)
